+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `billing/invoice.py`:
+  - `Line.vat` used `unit_price * rate`, ignoring quantity. It now uses `net * rate` (PRICING.md rule 3).
+  - `Invoice.add` now raises `ValueError` for a rate name not in `RATES` (rule 3).
+- `tests/test_invoice.py`: changed `test_reduced_rate_small_item`. It expected VAT 0.02 and gross 0.52 for a 0.50 item at the reduced rate. 0.50 × 0.05 = 0.025, which rule 4 says rounds half up to 0.03, so gross is 0.53. I believe the old expectation was wrong. It was the only test I edited.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest` before the changes: 4 failures. After: `Ran 6 tests ... OK`.
+- I checked the expected values in `test_quantity_applies_to_vat` and `test_mixed_rates` by hand against the rules. They match.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- The `test_reduced_rate_small_item` change rests on my reading of PRICING.md rule 4. It explicitly gives 0.025 → 0.03. If finance meant something else, that needs their confirmation.
+- I did not touch `docs/PRICING.md` or any file outside the allowed paths.
+- I added no new tests.
